+			for the kernel RNG using PKEYS. This feature hacks PKU to make
+			it available in the kernel and uses this isolation primitive
+			to secure various sensitive data in the kernel RNG which is
+			extracted into separate pages.
+
+config RNGUARD_MPK_SELFTEST
+	bool "Run boot-time self-tests for the RNGUARD pkeys defense"
+	depends on RNGUARD_MPK
+	help
+		Run a set of boot-time tests that verify the isolated .rnguard_iso
+		region behaves as intended. Results are reported via dmesg.
+
+		This is for debugging. Say N for production builds.
+
+config RNGUARD_MTE
+	bool "Enable MTE defense for RNGUARD"
+	depends on ARM64_MTE
+	help
+		Selecting this option provides integrity and confidentiality
+		for the kernel RNG using MTE for ARM64.
+
+config RNGUARD_MTE_SELFTEST
+	bool "Run boot-time self-tests for the RNGUARD MTE defense"
+	depends on RNGUARD_MTE
+	help
+		Run a set of boot-time tests that verify the isolated MTE
+		regions behave as intended. Results are reported via dmesg.
+
+		This is for debugging. Say N for production builds.
+
 menu "printk and dmesg options"
 
 config PRINTK_TIME
